# Bitwig Exact EQ / Device Parameter Tool

## Overview
This skill adds a new MCP tool that lets the agent set precise parameter values on any Bitwig device or audio effect (e.g., EQ frequency, gain, Q, filter cutoff, reverb decay). It extends the Java bridge with a new `/api/device/parameter` endpoint, adds a Python client method, registers the tool in the MCP server, and provides a clean interface for exact parameter control.

## When to Use
- The user asks to EQ a track with specific numbers (e.g., "cut 2kHz by 3dB", "set high shelf to 8kHz").
- The user wants to tweak a device parameter by exact value instead of browsing presets.
- The user needs to automate or batch-program device parameters across multiple tracks.

## Core Pattern / Instructions

### 1. Add the Java bridge endpoint
Edit `java-extension/src/main/java/com/bitwig/agent/BridgeHttpServer.java`:

